  "summary_en": "Georgia Senate Bill 219 would amend Title 40 to allow automated-driving-system vehicles on public roads without a human driver, treating the manufacturer as driver/operator. It creates \"SAVE projects\" with notice to local authorities, data recording, annual reporting, insurance, manufacturer liability, and preempts local regulation.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Manufacturer is deemed driver/operator when the ADS is engaged; no human presence required.",
   "SAVE projects require submission to Department of Revenue and one month's notice to local authorities.",
   "Vehicles need crash notification technology, data recording system, and minimum insurance.",
   "Manufacturer liable for damages when ADS engaged and vehicle caused the damage.",
   "Local governments barred from imposing fees or regulations on SAVE projects; manufacturer misdemeanor for violations."
  ],
